uying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Bally's Corporation is a fast-growing global entertainment brand with 20 casinos across 11 U.S. states and one casino in Newcastle, U.K., along with a golf course in New York and horse racetracks in Colorado and forthcoming in Wyoming. Bally's also owns Bally Bet, a first-in-class sports betting and igaming platform licensed in 16 jurisdictions in North America. Bally's holds a majority interest in Bally's Intralot S.A., a leading lottery solutions supplier and gaming operator active in 39 jurisdictions worldwide. Bally's casino operations include approximately 17,700 slot machines, 630 table games, and 3,950 hotel rooms. Bally's also has rights to developable land in Las Vegas at the site of the former Tropicana Las Vegas, has been awarded a license to build a full-scale casino and resort in The Bronx, New York, and an integrated destination resort in Chicago, Illinois. The firm has over 12,000 employees across the world, recognized for their innovation, energy, and dedication to creating thrilling gaming experiences. Bally's Corporation was incorporated in 2004 in Delaware.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robeson Mandela Reeves | CEO & Director | Age 41 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 11K people. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Bally's Corporation is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $625M market cap.","The top line has compounded at +23% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $86M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Carries a 121% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.206467885776056},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 53/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Cyclical peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How (BALY) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.co